Subject: [PATCH] JSC: restore the MIPS32 assembler, LLInt and baseline JIT

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [restores a backend removed upstream in 272866@main]

WebKit removed the MIPS assembler, MacroAssembler, offlineasm backend and the
MIPS paths of LLInt, the JIT and YARR in January 2024 (272866@main) and moved
MIPS to C_LOOP. This brings them back on top of 2.54 for MIPS32 little endian,
o32, hard float, release 1 (-march=mips32), with the baseline JIT and the YARR
JIT; DFG, FTL and WebAssembly stay disabled.

- assembler: MIPSAssembler, MIPSRegisters, MacroAssemblerMIPS restored and
  brought to the 2.54 interface (ASCIILiteral register names, RepatchingInfo,
  movz/movn, 8/16 bit extensions and ctz without release 2 instructions,
  conditional moves, transfers, branch16, Float16 and vector stubs as on ARMv7).
- offlineasm: mips.rb restored and adapted (LocalLabel.unique, writefence,
  t6 and ft6/ft7 registers); the LLInt register block for MIPS maps a0-a3,
  r0/r1 and fa0/fa1 to the o32 registers.
- LLInt: callee saves s0/s1/s4, the 16 byte o32 argument area in the native,
  internal function and host call trampolines, stack alignment at VM entry.
- JIT: GPRInfo/FPRInfo for 2.54 (the handler register t6 is outside the
  preferred argument registers), register sets, CCallHelpers o32 argument
  placement, function prologue, DataIC prologue, CallFrameShuffler, the o32
  argument area in the native call thunk, YARR registers and fifth argument.

